  "boundary": "Exact selected registration and module/token joins establish direct source order and structural-only framing. The member28 action preserves two targets, curve, direction, BlackboardImpactValue, four independently nullable BlackboardDouble profiles and every intervening byte/scalar in the recorded order. The concrete Impact member4 reader has byte payload, byte, DWORD and final byte, permitting reuse of the scalar-flag-payload grammar while keeping type identity distinct. The helper320D4B0 consumes exactly one source byte, independent of the enum type name. Header availability checks are not member counts. Existing target/direction/curve and four-byte Double profiles retain their selected native evidence (buff_24_native.json and buff_35_native.json). Count bounds precede multiplication/iteration; arbitrary scalar bits and independent null states remain preserved. Normal, FF, lazy, formatter, allocation and existing-output paths retain complete instructions. Hurt animation behavior, impact meaning, target ownership, live formatter selection, complete refill/error parity and whole-BuffData EOF remain unresolved."
